 "subject": "Friday, Nov 13 - Morning edition",
 "body": "<style>@import url(\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IM+Fell+English&family=Pinyon+Script&family=Source+Serif+4:opsz,wght@8..60,400;8..60,600&display=swap\");a[x-apple-data-detectors]{color:inherit!important;text-decoration:none!important;font-size:inherit!important;font-family:inherit!important;font-weight:inherit!important;line-height:inherit!important}.hd-wrap,.hd-inner{background-color:#2c2c2e!important;color:#d1d1d6!important}.hd-root,.hd-wrap{width:100%!important;min-width:100%!important}.hd-inner{width:100%!important;max-width:600px!important;margin:0 auto!important}.hd-body{overflow-wrap:break-word;word-wrap:break-word}img{max-width:100%;height:auto}h3.hd-ink::first-letter{float:left;font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-weight:400;color:#e08a6f;font-size:2.6em;line-height:.85;padding:.05em .1em 0 0;margin:0 .1em .05em 0}.newsletter-body,.email-content,body{width:100%!important;min-width:100%!important;margin:0!important;padding:0!important}@media (max-width:480px){.hd-seal,.hd-seal-t{width:104px!important;max-width:104px!important}.hd-seal{height:104px!important}}@media (max-width:400px){.hd-wm-p{font-size:21px!important;letter-spacing:.5px!important}.hd-wm-s{font-size:26px!important;margin:0 2px!important}}</style>\n<div class=\"hd-root\" style=\"width:100%;min-width:100%;margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#2c2c2e\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" class=\"hd-wrap\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" bgcolor=\"#2c2c2e\" style=\"width:100%;min-width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background-color:#2c2c2e\"><tr><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" bgcolor=\"#2c2c2e\" style=\"padding:0;background-color:#2c2c2e;text-align:center\"><center><!--[if mso]><table role=\"presentation\" width=\"600\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\"><tr><td><![endif]--><table role=\"presentation\" class=\"hd-inner\" width=\"100%\" align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" bgcolor=\"#2c2c2e\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:600px;border-collapse:collapse;background-color:#2c2c2e;margin:0 auto;text-align:left\"><tr><td class=\"hd-body\" bgcolor=\"#2c2c2e\" style=\"padding:6px 16px 20px;background-color:#2c2c2e;color:#d1d1d6;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;text-align:left;overflow-wrap:break-word;word-wrap:break-word\">\n<p class=\"hd-inkrule hd-ink\" style=\"margin:0;padding:6px 0 5px;border-top:3px double #f2f2f7;border-bottom:1px solid #f2f2f7;text-align:center;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:9px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#f2f2f7\">Spin-free news · Ranked by impact</p>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding:24px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0;font-size:0\"><table role=\"presentation\" class=\"hd-seal-t\" align=\"center\" width=\"140\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:140px;margin:0 auto;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td align=\"center\" valign=\"top\" style=\"text-align:center;line-height:0;font-size:0;padding:0\"><a href=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/\" style=\"display:block;text-align:center;margin:0 auto;text-decoration:none;border:0\"><img class=\"hd-seal\" src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/seal.png\" alt=\"High Impact News Daily\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" border=\"0\" style=\"display:block;margin:0 auto;width:140px;max-width:100%;height:auto;border:0;outline:none;text-decoration:none\"></a></td></tr></table></td></tr></table>\n<p style=\"margin:12px 0 0;text-align:center;white-space:nowrap;line-height:1.1\"><a href=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/\" style=\"text-decoration:none\"><span class=\"hd-ink hd-wm-p\" style=\"font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:25px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#f2f2f7\">HIGH</span> <span class=\"hd-accent hd-wm-s\" style=\"font-family:'Pinyon Script','Snell Roundhand',cursive;font-size:31px;margin:0 3px;color:#e08a6f\">impact</span> <span class=\"hd-ink hd-wm-p\" style=\"font-family:'IM Fell English',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:25px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#f2f2f7\">NEWS</span> <span class=\"hd-accent hd-wm-s\" style=\"font-family:'Pinyon Script','Snell Roundhand',cursive;font-size:31px;margin:0 3px;color:#e08a6f\">daily</span></a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:8px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-head.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:260px;max-width:80%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n\n<p class=\"hd-accent\" style=\"margin:18px 0 0;text-align:center;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#e08a6f\">Morning edition · Friday, November 13</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:4px 0 6px;text-align:center;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-style:italic;font-size:14px;color:#8e8e93\">What happened overnight, and yesterday&#x27;s biggest stories. Five minutes. No spin.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:26px 0 0;padding:0 0 6px;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8e8e93\">Overnight</p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:20px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Microsoft&#x27;s Outlook and Teams outage ran into a second day Friday, with fixes failing and governments and companies worldwide still affected.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">The disruption began about 11:17 a.m. ET Thursday, according to Microsoft&#x27;s service health dashboard, and more than 130,000 users reported problems that day. Microsoft said overnight its latest fixes were &quot;not taking as expected&quot; and that some restored servers became unresponsive again once traffic returned; it has given no time for full recovery. Exchange Online mail was hit hardest, with Exchange-dependent Teams calendar and scheduling features also failing. Officials in Singapore, Japan and Australia reported impacts, and Microsoft said there was no indication of malicious activity.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> Outlook and Teams carry the workday for hundreds of millions of people, and a second day of outage hits Friday business. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/microsoft-outage-outlook-email-365-status-down-d92547a821930290db2964388016979a\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Associated Press ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Iran&#x27;s Revolutionary Guards said they struck a U.S. early-warning radar in Bahrain, their first claimed attack on a Gulf country since September.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">The Guards said the strike, reported by Iranian state media Friday, retaliated for what they called an air attack on a telecommunications tower in Sirik in southern Hormozgan province, and called it a &quot;serious warning&quot; to the U.S. The Guards also said a liquefied petroleum gas tanker hit a mine in the Strait of Hormuz after ignoring warnings. Neither claim could be independently verified, and the U.S. and Bahrain, home of the Navy&#x27;s 5th Fleet, had not commented. The claims come during a fragile lull in the war that began Feb. 28.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> A confirmed hit on a U.S. asset would break the lull in the Iran war. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/irans-guards-say-they-targeted-us-early-warning-radar-bahrain-2026-11-13/\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Reuters ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Sen. Chris Van Hollen said he will challenge Chuck Schumer to lead the new Democratic Senate majority, calling for &quot;new leadership.&quot;</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">The Maryland Democrat announced Thursday night that he will run for majority leader in a closed-door, secret-ballot caucus vote next month (Dec. 1, per CNN). &quot;It&#x27;s now on us to meet this moment, and to do that we need new leadership,&quot; he said. Schumer, Democratic leader since 2017, said he has &quot;the votes to continue serving as Democratic Leader.&quot; Van Hollen said he has more than 10 commitments and called himself the underdog; Sen. Bernie Sanders and Sen.-elect Abdul El-Sayed back him, and Sen. Angus King backs Schumer. Democrats will hold at least 55 seats.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> The winner sets the agenda of the Senate majority that takes over in January. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/us/chris-van-hollen-announces-run-us-senate-majority-leader-challenging-schumer-2026-11-13/\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Reuters ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Democrat Cindy Holscher won the Kansas governor&#x27;s race, AP projected Thursday, keeping the office in her party&#x27;s hands.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">Holscher, a state senator, led Republican Ty Masterson, the Trump-endorsed state Senate president, 50.3% to 49.7% with 98% of votes counted when AP called the race at 5:43 p.m. ET, nine days after the election. It was the state&#x27;s closest governor&#x27;s race since 1974, and Kansas had never before elected back-to-back Democratic governors; she succeeds term-limited Gov. Laura Kelly. Masterson conceded in a statement. Democrats had already secured a majority of U.S. governorships for the first time in two decades.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> It adds to the Democrats&#x27; midterm wave in a state that usually votes Republican. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/kansas-governor-midterm-election-cindy-holscher-c9bb46dfd593fa7182a6bc93722ce552\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Associated Press ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">The Brooklyn apartment building collapse killed eight people, including two children, New York&#x27;s mayor said as the search for victims ended.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">The toll rose from two on Wednesday. Mayor Zohran Mamdani said two of the dead were construction workers and 18 people were hurt in the collapse and rescue. The three-story building on Flatbush Avenue gave way Wednesday afternoon while workers were digging at a neighboring lot; the cause is under investigation. The fire department ended rescue operations Thursday, and Mamdani ordered safety inspections at about 100 building sites tied to the companies involved in the construction project.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> It is New York&#x27;s deadliest building collapse in years and puts excavation next to occupied buildings under scrutiny. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/new-york-city-building-collapse-kills-8-mayor-expands-probe-2026-11-12/\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Reuters ↗</a></p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:34px 0 0;padding:14px 0 6px;border-top:3px double #48484a;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8e8e93\">Yesterday&#x27;s biggest stories</p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:20px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang resigned effective immediately, and finance chief Colette Kress will serve as interim CEO while the board searches for a successor.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">Nvidia&#x27;s board said Thursday it accepted Huang&#x27;s resignation as president, CEO and director; it will consider internal and external candidates. Kress, CFO since 2013, keeps that job while serving as interim CEO. Harvey C. Jones, a former Synopsys CEO on the board since 1993, was named Nvidia&#x27;s first-ever board chair. The resignation follows Huang&#x27;s admission Sunday of an affair with a Megaspeed executive whom U.S. officials believe is a Chinese spy, and a New York Times report of a second relationship with an Nvidia executive who reports to him. Nvidia shares fell as much as 14% Thursday before recovering about half of that loss, the Associated Press reported. Nvidia still plans to report quarterly results Tuesday, Nov. 17.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-4.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 4/5.</b> Huang founded Nvidia in 1993 and led it to the center of the AI boom as the world&#x27;s most valuable chipmaker. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/11/12/3401635/0/en/nvidia-announces-ceo-transition.html\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">NVIDIA (company release) ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Nvidia&#x27;s board met late Wednesday to decide whether to remove CEO Jensen Huang, and its shares fell about 6% before the market opened Thursday.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">CNBC confirmed the meeting after The Wall Street Journal reported the board was preparing to oust Huang; no decision had been announced by early Thursday. The New York Times reported Wednesday that Huang had a second extramarital relationship, with an Nvidia executive who reports to him; Huang admitted on Sunday to an affair with a Megaspeed executive whom U.S. intelligence officials believe is a Chinese spy, and the board opened an investigation. Nvidia&#x27;s bylaws let a majority of its 11 directors remove the CEO. Shares were down 6.3% in premarket trading at 4:34 a.m. ET, after falling more than 8% after hours Wednesday; Bernstein cut its price target to $200 from $400.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-4.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 4/5.</b> Nvidia is the world&#x27;s most valuable chipmaker and the center of the AI boom, and Huang has led it since founding it in 1993. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/12/nvidia-nvda-jensen-huang-second-affair.html\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">CNBC ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Microsoft&#x27;s Outlook, Teams and other 365 services went down for hours Thursday, with more than 130,000 Outlook problem reports at the peak.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">Downdetector logged more than 130,000 Outlook reports at 1:27 p.m. ET, Reuters reported. Microsoft said a large number of servers became unexpectedly unavailable after failing automated health checks, pushing load onto the rest of its systems; it paused all deployments and configuration changes and restarted servers. Exchange Online, Teams, SharePoint Online, Microsoft 365 Copilot and Defender XDR were listed as affected. As of about 4 p.m. ET Microsoft said a new health-check method was returning servers to service and was being applied more broadly, and that recent configuration updates were a potential cause still under investigation.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> Hundreds of millions of workers rely on Outlook and Teams for email and meetings. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.reuters.com/technology/microsoft-365-outlook-down-thousands-us-users-downdetector-shows-2026-11-12/\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Reuters ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">President Trump said the U.S. does not need a deal with Iran, days after saying talks to end the war were progressing; oil prices rose.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">&quot;We don&#x27;t need a deal with Iran. Those days have long since passed. We&#x27;ve got their money, Hundreds of Billions of Dollars, and we&#x27;ve got their Strait!&quot; Trump wrote on Truth Social Thursday. On Sunday he had said new strikes were highly unlikely as talks progressed. Brent crude rose 1.9% to $94.48 a barrel and U.S. crude 2% to $88.19 during the day, CNBC reported; both had fallen sharply in November on hopes the war was ending.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> The post casts doubt on talks to end the U.S.-Iran war and the shipping disruption in the Strait of Hormuz. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/12/oil-prices-jump-after-trump-says-no-iran-deal-needed-weve-got-their-strait.html\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">CNBC ↗</a></p>\n<p style=\"margin:22px 0 0;text-align:center;line-height:0\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/orn-sep.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" style=\"display:inline-block;width:180px;max-width:60%;height:auto;border:0\"></p>\n<h3 class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"margin:22px 0 8px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:18px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:600;color:#f2f2f7\">Indonesia&#x27;s Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka resigned after court rulings found his overseas high-school credentials fell short of legal requirements.</h3>\n<p class=\"hd-body\" style=\"margin:0 0 10px;font-family:'Source Serif 4','Source Serif Pro',Georgia,'Times New Roman',Times,serif;font-size:15px;line-height:1.5;color:#d1d1d6\">Gibran, 39, the son of former President Joko Widodo, handed his resignation letter to the People&#x27;s Consultative Assembly on Thursday, a day after 120 lawmakers began an impeachment push. President Prabowo Subianto said he accepted it &quot;with a heavy heart.&quot; Gibran said the decision was personal and his documents were complete. The assembly must elect a replacement within 60 days from two candidates the president nominates. The rupiah hit a record low of 18,255 per dollar, Reuters reported.</p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted\" style=\"margin:0;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px;line-height:1.45;color:#8e8e93\"><img src=\"https://hinewsdaily.com/assets/email/impact-3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" style=\"width:50px;max-width:100%;height:auto;vertical-align:-3px;border:0\"> <b class=\"hd-ink\" style=\"color:#f2f2f7\">Impact 3/5.</b> It is Indonesia&#x27;s highest-profile resignation since President Suharto quit in 1998. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/indonesia-vp-gibran-hands-his-resignation-upper-house-2026-11-12/\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Reuters ↗</a></p>\n<p class=\"hd-muted hd-rule\" style=\"margin:34px 0 0;padding:14px 0 6px;border-top:3px double #48484a;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:1.6px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8e8e93\">This week so far</p>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td class=\"hd-body hd-rule\" style=\"padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;color:#d1d1d6\">Democrat Scott Colom won Mississippi&#x27;s U.S. Senate race, defeating Republican Sen. Cindy Hyde-Smith and becoming the state&#x27;s first Black senator since Reconstruction. <a class=\"hd-accent\" href=\"https://apnews.com/article/scott-colom-mississippi-senate-midterms-56c18f292a734443992f9466c3b0f346\" style=\"color:#e08a6f;text-decoration:none;font-weight:600\">Source ↗</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"hd-body hd-rule\" style=\"padding:9px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #48484a;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Helvetica Neue',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;color:#d1d1d6\">The resolution to impeach Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth was sent to the House Judiciary Committee on a 211-204 vote, blocking a floor vote on removing him. <a class=\"hd-accent\" h